# drizzle-kit owns these: it rewrites meta/_journal.json in full on every
# `drizzle-kit generate` and writes each snapshot verbatim. Prettier
# reformatting them breaks byte-reproducibility from the generator — the next
# migration would silently revert them to drizzle-kit's own style, replaying
# the exact drift this sweep exists to clean up.
apps/server/drizzle/meta/*.json
# Same generator-ownership reason, plus 0003_outstanding_doctor_spectrum.sql
# is hand-edited with a `NOT VALID` clause drizzle-kit cannot emit. No SQL
# prettier plugin is installed today so these aren't reformatted regardless —
# ignored explicitly so a future plugin can't reintroduce the drift.
apps/server/drizzle/*.sql

# apps/server/scripts/generate-reference-data.ts owns these: its
# `toJsonLines()` deliberately writes one record per line ("compact but
# diffable" — its own comment). Reformatting to multi-line-per-object now
# would revert on the next generator run, replaying the exact drift this
# sweep exists to clean up.
apps/server/reference-data/*.json

